  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Pages and navigation",
      "items": [
        "The hub lists every semester, subject and chapter. Its review board ranks started chapters by due date from each chapter's -checks and -log keys, and it draws the route line and the radar from the same progress. (js/index.js:46–60, 99–119, 370–422)",
        "Each guide links to its lab and back. The contents rail fetches the hub's index.html once per session, keeps the chapter list in sessionStorage, and adds a Chapters fold and a previous/next pager; opened as a file without the hub it adds nothing. (js/nav.js:195–216, 288–306)",
        "How to use and the Version log live in about/ and are linked from the hub footer and the settings panel. (index.html:214; js/settings.js:118)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Progress stays in the browser",
      "items": [
        "There is no server or account. Guides save ticks as <key>-checks and review days as <key>-log; labs save answers as <key>-lab and tick lab-<id> in the same -checks key, so the hub counts both. (js/guide.js:1–25; js/lab.js:1–9)",
        "Settings (theme, motion, text size) save as site-settings and apply from the <head> before the page paints; settings.js also loads the HUD layer, hud.js. Storage errors are swallowed, so nothing persists where storage is blocked. (js/settings.js:1–33)",
        "Lab experiments are per-chapter scripts that register with window.Lab; their physics modules also load in node for the tests. (js/lab.js:334–343; js/eei/ch1-physics.js:1–3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authoring and publishing",
      "items": [
        "Guide HTML is the single source: guide-to-tex.py writes the .tex and latexmk builds the PDF, both committed next to the guide; check-guide.py fails when they are stale. (tools/guide-to-tex.py:1–6; tools/check-guide.py:280–288)",
        "GitHub Pages publishes main from the root on every push. The Jekyll site CI workflow only builds the site as a check; it does not publish. (README.md:179–185; .github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1–19)",
        "Google Fonts serves Hanken Grotesk to every page; the hub is shown as the representative caller. (index.html:19)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}